{"data":{"print":{"id":"841565","name":"Tall skirts mod for Voron 0.2","slug":"tall-skirts-mod-for-voron-02","description":"<p>I wanted to have taller skirts on my Voron 0.2 so i could place the electronics on the bottom. To achieve this I made the feet taller and adapted the skirts. The skirts have roughly the same heigt as the skirts of a V2.4 or Voron Trident, but smaller hexagons.</p><p>All files are available as stls, which have already the correct printing orientation and as step files.</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.printables.com/media/prints/841565/rich_content/050a6182-bc09-4a52-865a-8bd2e543def3/bildschirmfoto-2024-05-15-um-203426.png#%7B%22uuid%22%3A%22e18cb055-3061-48d9-b333-0f7433b936bc%22%2C%22w%22%3A2132%2C%22h%22%3A1646%7D\"></figure><h3>The mod consists of</h3><h4>Front feet</h4><p>The front feet are only taller and have no additional changes.</p><ul><li>Tall_Foot_Front_Right_x1.stl</li><li>Tall_Foot_Front_Left_x1.stl</li></ul><h4>Rear right foot</h4><p>There are two versions available. One plan foot and one with the integrated filament sensor.</p><ul><li>Tall_Foot_Rear_Right_Plain_x1.stl</li><li>Tall_Foot_Rear_Right_FRS_x1.stl</li></ul><h4>Rear left foot</h4><p>There are four version available. Two for a 24v input and two for the V0.2 bom mains inlet. For each version you can choose between a version with a cutout for a RJ45 keystone adapter and one without.</p><ul><li>Tall_Foot_Rear_Left_Mains_Inlet_x1.stl (Bom Mains inlet no RJ45 cutout)</li><li>Tall_Foot_Rear_Left_Mains_Inlet_RJ45_x1.stl (Bom Mains inlet RJ45 cutout)</li><li>Tall_Foot_Rear_Left_24V_Inlet_x1.stl (24V version no RJ45 cutout)</li><li>Tall_Foot_Rear_Left_24V_Inlet_RJ45_x1.stl (24V version RJ45 cutout)</li></ul><p>Also there is a small lid that you can screw on that hides the mains connections.</p><figure class=\"image image_resized\" style=\"width:50%;\"><img src=\"https://media.printables.com/media/prints/841565/rich_content/b0ce4625-0504-4543-a5ab-d929dc26d931/bildschirmfoto-2024-05-15-um-103428.png#%7B%22uuid%22%3A%22b03ca53c-ff02-4500-a000-6f71ea9a336a%22%2C%22w%22%3A1726%2C%22h%22%3A1528%7D\"></figure><h3>Skirts</h3><p>There are two skirt versions available. Plain skirts and skirts that can be printed with a mesh behind the normal hexagons. The mesh versions are 1mm thicker, so the \u201cinfill\u201d mesh can be applied in the slicer\"</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td>without mesh</td><td>with mesh</td></tr><tr><td><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.printables.com/media/prints/841565/rich_content/aa2ea3c3-1417-4c36-bb65-c94d39159b83/bildschirmfoto-2024-05-15-um-214107.png#%7B%22uuid%22%3A%22b1b46239-9384-4aac-a26b-87ddbb505699%22%2C%22w%22%3A1622%2C%22h%22%3A1082%7D\"></figure></td><td><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.printables.com/media/prints/841565/rich_content/46e2fa86-68bf-45d0-9099-1e742299a6ee/bildschirmfoto-2024-05-15-um-214016.png#%7B%22uuid%22%3A%22eba1819d-f3e3-4b4a-8ebe-c1ef7ded4a02%22%2C%22w%22%3A1622%2C%22h%22%3A1082%7D\"></figure></td></tr></tbody></table></figure><h4>Front Skirt</h4><ul><li>Tall_Front_Skirt_x1.stl together with [a]_Logo_Insert_x2.stl</li><li>Tall_Front_Skirt_Mesh_x1.stl together with [a]_Logo_Insert_Mesh_x2.stl</li><li>Waveshare_4.3_DSI_LCD_Faceplate.stl</li></ul><h4>Side Skirts</h4><ul><li>Tall_Side_Skirt_x2.stl</li><li>Tall_Side_Skirt_Mesh_x2</li></ul><h4>Rear Skirt</h4><ul><li>Tall_Rear_Skirt_x1.stl</li><li>Tall_Rear_Skirt_Mesh_x1.stl</li></ul><h4>Bottom Panel</h4><ul><li>Bottom_Panel_Mesh.stl</li></ul><h3>Printing instructions</h3><p>As stated in the Voron documentation:</p><ul><li>ABS</li><li>0.2mm layer hight</li><li>0.4mm extrusion width</li><li>40% infill</li><li>wall count 4</li><li>top/bottom layers 5</li><li>no supports</li></ul><p>For the meshed skirts I used the following settings:</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.printables.com/media/prints/841565/rich_content/cbfd9aef-6643-4723-abf8-4c949fcbcda5/bildschirmfoto-2024-05-15-um-213917.png#%7B%22uuid%22%3A%225a7729df-8da8-442d-9dee-3a4c0291cb3d%22%2C%22w%22%3A3440%2C%22h%22%3A2056%7D\"></figure><p>Object is placed at 45\u00b0 on the build plate. I did also a (manual) filament swap for the mesh. You don't necessarily need to do that.</p><p>For the meshed bottom panel the follogin settings were used (mesh from 0-0.8mm) :</p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.printables.com/media/prints/841565/rich_content/8dbd80dd-d4c2-43c8-8224-ff2269585cb1/bildschirmfoto-2024-05-15-um-215842.png#%7B%22uuid%22%3A%22b1f4d6c7-a18f-444d-aad8-3f284900a3cd%22%2C%22w%22%3A3448%2C%22h%22%3A2064%7D\"></figure><figure class=\"image\"><img></figure><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"https://media.printables.com/media/prints/841565/rich_content/85df1153-64dd-4233-a540-f8b8d9f67ecd/bildschirmfoto-2024-05-15-um-221951.png#%7B%22uuid%22%3A%22379136c7-3348-4528-90d8-035d5bd783f5%22%2C%22w%22%3A3448%2C%22h%22%3A2064%7D\"></figure><p>The bottom panel is placed at 90\u00b0 on the build plate. I did not do a color swap for the bottom panel.</p><h3>BOM</h3><p>These parts are needed in addition to the bom for the standard skirts</p><ul><li>4 x M2.5x6 BHCS (to mount the Waveshare Display to the front skirt)</li><li>6x M2x6 SHCS or BHCS (optional - for additional stability of the skirts)</li><li>2x M3x5 BHCS (rear skirt)</li><li>2x M3x6 BHCS (needed to secure RJ45 keystone insert)</li><li>2x M3x16 BHCS (mains cover)</li><li>4x M3 Threaded inserts (right rear foot 1x, left rear foot 3x)</li></ul><p>For the 24V version of the rear left foot i used:</p><ul><li>KPJX-PM-4S (<a href=\"https://www.digikey.de/de/products/detail/kycon-inc/KPJX-PM-4S/9990081\">https://www.digikey.de/de/products/detail/kycon-inc/KPJX-PM-4S/9990081</a>)</li><li>DC capable SWITCH ROCKER SPST 10A 250V (<a href=\"https://www.digikey.de/de/products/detail/w%C3%BCrth-elektronik/471002268142/9950821\">https://www.digikey.de/de/products/detail/w%C3%BCrth-elektronik/471002268142/9950821</a>)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p>","summary":"Taller skirts mod for Voron 0.2","modified":"2024-05-16T19:38:43.821078+00:00","firstPublish":"2024-05-15T20:00:47.550050+00:00","datePublished":"2024-05-16T19:38:43.804036+00:00","filesCount":45,"filesType":null,"pdfFilePath":"media/prints/841565/pdfs/841565-tall-skirts-mod-for-voron-02-bd7f4090-c36d-4715-9653-f899303fceb8.pdf","user":{"id":"145063","handle":"Akio","publicUsername":"Akio"},"license":{"id":"12","name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","disallowRemixing":false},"stls":[{"id":"3712558","name":"Tall_Foot_Front_Right_x1.stl","fileSize":1042584,"filePreviewPath":"media/prints/841565/previews/28dcc265f399b27c6c0aca50be098856420ca50c.png","created":"2024-05-15T18:40:39.073514+00:00","modified":"2024-05-15T19:46:46.884320+00:00","folder":"Feet","note":"","order":0,"formatColor":null},{"id":"3712522","name":"Tall_Foot_Front_Right_x1.step","fileSize":370819,"filePreviewPath":"media/prints/841565/previews/1edbfb66-948a-41c9-841f-3e28e78d4a93.png","created":"2024-05-15T18:40:28.612727+00:00","modified":"2024-05-15T19:46:46.915814+00:00","folder":"Feet","note":"","order":1,"formatColor":null},{"id":"3712531","name":"Tall_Foot_Front_Left_x1.stl","fileSize":1043284,"filePreviewPath":"media/prints/841565/previews/7b64ce694096eab5bd7b4c76beb5f0410f1549e0.png","created":"2024-05-15T18:40:30.916685+00:00","modified":"2024-05-15T19:46:46.895247+00:00","folder":"Feet","note":"","order":2,"formatColor":null},{"id":"3712520","name":"Tall_Foot_Front_Left_x1.step","fileSize":373366,"filePreviewPath":"media/prints/841565/previews/53531d1c-4d81-4b63-abe5-2f604b98dd10.png","created":"2024-05-15T18:40:27.650671+00:00","modified":"2024-05-15T19:46:46.909091+00:00","folder":"Feet","note":"","order":3,"formatColor":null},{"id":"3712543","name":"Tall_Foot_Rear_Right_Plain_x1.stl","fileSize":608584,"filePreviewPath":"media/prints/841565/previews/10255317d962b85470dbf87e11e15df504354517.png","created":"2024-05-15T18:40:34.688226+00:00","mod